<h1>Azerbaijani Subcategorization  Grammar</h1>Version of September 11, 2026, 12:47 pm<br />Documentation available at <a href="http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar" target="_blank">http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar</a><br />Tagset available at <a href="../dictionary/export_tagset.php" target="_blank">Export UNDL Foundation tagset</a>.<br /><br /><b>Y0</b><br />AVALENT<br /><br /><b>Y1</b><br />NO SUBCATEGORIZATION FRAME: rules defined inside the entry in the dictionary<br /><br /><b>Y42</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase (<i>O güldü.</i>)<br />VS(NP);
<br /><br /><b>Y43</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, and a verb complement, which is also a noun phrase (<i>O nahar(i) yeyir.</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP);
VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC);
<br /><br /><b>Y44</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase,two verb complements, which are accusative (-i) and dative (-a) NPs.
 (<i>Mən kitabı sənə verdim</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(NP,DAT);
<br /><br /><b>Y45</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, and a verb complement which is a complementizer phrase headed by "ki" (<i>Mən dedim ki...</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(CH([ki]));
<br /><br /><b>Y46</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, and a verb complement which is a noun phrase, adjective phrase or prepositional phrase deaded by -da/-dan 

 (<i>O tələbə dir, Evdə dir</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC({NP|JP|PH([{da|dan}])});
<br /><br /><b>Y47</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, a verb complement, and also a verb complement which is a complementizer phrase headed by 'ki' (<i>O bizə əmr elədi ki...</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(CH([ki]));
<br /><br /><b>Y48</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, and a verb complement, which is an adjective phrase.



 (<i>Mən yorğun görünürəm</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(JP);
<br /><br /><b>Y49</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, a verb complement which is a dative NP (-a), and also a verb complement which is an adjective phrase (<i>O Həsənə pis davrandı</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,DAT)VC(JP);
<br /><br /><b>Y50</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is an accusative noun phrase (-i),a verb complement, which is NP and also a verb complement which is a PP. (<i>kitabı qoydum masa üstünə</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PH([{ə|də|dən}]));
<br /><br /><b>Y51</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, and a verb complement, which is a dative noun phrase (-a) (<i>arzulamaq</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,DAT);
<br /><br /><b>Y52</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, and a verb complement, which is an accusative noun phrase (-i) (<i>aldatmaq</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC);
<br /><br /><b>Y53</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, and a verb complement, which is a  locative noun phrase (-da) (<i>çimmək</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,LOC);
<br /><br /><b>Y54</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase, and a verb complement, which is an ablative noun phrase (-dan) (<i>ayrılmaq</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ABL);
<br /><br /><b>Y56</b><br />requires a verb specifier, which is a noun phrase,two verb complements, which are accusative (-i) and ablative (-dan) NPs. \r\n\r\n (<i>Mən onu işdən kənar etdim</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(NP,ABL);
